The Edit menu depends on the document, as {x:view-make-kind} says: it has
Title; Structured (unstructured document) or Unstructured (a document that is
one section); Section (or Document while one section is shown); and Window.

.h3 Quit [view-quit]
.ix Shell, no exit to a shell
.ix Quit (menu entry)
.ix Quit, unsaved changes
.ix Discard changes
.ix Ctrl-Q
The Editor has no entry that leaves it for a shell.  Open another terminal
or window to use a shell.

{b:Quit} (or {k:Ctrl-Q}) leaves the Editor.  If the document has unsaved
changes (the asterisk before its name) a list headed {c:Document has unsaved
changes} is shown first:

.table 22 38
Entry | Effect
Save and quit | Save the document under its own name, then leave.  If the
 | save fails the Editor stays.
Discard changes and quit | Leave without saving.
Cancel | Stay.  ({k:Esc} does the same.)
.end
The hint of the Quit entry shows "Return to the Document Manager".  When the
Document Manager started the Editor, that is what happens.  When the Editor
was started on its own, it ends and the terminal prompt or the desktop
returns.  The close button of the X11 window acts as {k:Ctrl-Q}.

.h2 Accelerators [view-accel]
.ix Accelerators
.ix Ctrl keys
.ix Shortcuts
.ix Command shortcuts
An accelerator is a Ctrl letter that does at once what a menu or a
